## Interview Questions (Trading Systems)

> **Q**: "How do you prevent a bug from placing infinite orders?"
> **A**: Rate limiters (8 req/sec), position limits (hard caps), circuit breakers (auto-disable after N failures), kill switch (manual override), cooldown periods (prevent rapid trades)

> **Q**: "What's look-ahead bias and why does it invalidate backtests?"
> **A**: Using future data to make past decisions; makes strategies look profitable when they're not. Example: Using today's closing price to decide yesterday's trade.

> **Q**: "How do you handle API rate limits in a trading system?"
> **A**: Token bucket rate limiter (8 tokens/sec), request queuing, exponential backoff on 429 errors, circuit breaker to stop trading if API is down

> **Q**: "Why use Decimal instead of float for money calculations?"
> **A**: Float precision errors: `0.1 + 0.2 = 0.30000000000000004`. Decimal maintains exact precision for financial calculations.

